cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyMCNP in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "PyMCNP: Python tools for creating, validating, running, and analyzing MCNP simulations"
abstract: >-
  PyMCNP is a Python package and command-line interface for the Monte Carlo
  N-Particle (MCNP) code. It parses, creates, validates, and writes MCNP input
  files, reads OUTP, MESHTAL, and PTRAC output files, and provides utilities to
  check inputs, convert and plot tallies, run simulations in parallel, and
  visualize cell and surface geometries.
